### File Structure

```
ExpenseTracker/
│
├── data/
│   ├── users.txt
│   ├── expenses.txt
│   └── income.txt
│
├── templates/
│   ├── login.html
│   ├── register.html
│   ├── dashboard.html
│   ├── add_expense.html
│   ├── add_income.html
│   ├── view_expenses.html
│   └── reports.html
│
├── static/
│   ├── css/
│   │   └── styles.css
│   └── js/
│       └── scripts.js
│
└── app.py
```

### File Descriptions

```
- ExpenseTracker/: Root directory for the ExpenseTracker web application.

- data/: Directory to store local text files for user authentication, expenses, and income records.
  - users.txt: Stores user credentials in the format `username:password`.
  - expenses.txt: Stores expense records in the format `date|name|amount|category`.
  - income.txt: Stores income records in the format `date|amount|category`.

- templates/: Directory containing HTML templates for the web application.
  - login.html: HTML template for the user login page.
  - register.html: HTML template for the user registration page.
  - dashboard.html: HTML template for the expense dashboard page.
  - add_expense.html: HTML template for the add new expense page.
  - add_income.html: HTML template for the add new income page.
  - view_expenses.html: HTML template for the view all expenses page.
  - reports.html: HTML template for the expense reports page.

- static/: Directory for static files such as CSS and JavaScript.
  - css/: Directory for CSS files.
    - styles.css: CSS file for styling the web application.
  - js/: Directory for JavaScript files.
    - scripts.js: JavaScript file for client-side functionality.

- app.py: Main Python file containing the backend code for the ExpenseTracker application, handling routing, user authentication, data management, and rendering templates.
```

